        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Clarify else-if evaluation order]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43917</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43917"/>
        <updated>2026-04-23T20:42:16.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142841841?u=54af0059828b660824039be2a41e622636c03edf&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Clarifies the <code class="notranslate">if...else if...else</code> description to explicitly state that conditions are evaluated in order and that the rest of the chain is skipped after the first condition evaluates to <code class="notranslate">true</code>.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">The page explained the syntax and nesting of <code class="notranslate">else if</code>, but it did not clearly state that later branches are not evaluated once an earlier condition matches. Adding this makes the control flow behavior easier to understand for readers.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<p dir="auto">This is a small documentation-only clarification in the main <code class="notranslate">if...else</code> reference page.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #43891.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4306411704" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43891" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/43891/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43891">#43891</a></p>]]></content>
